From: Hynek Moravec <hynek.moravec@hardwario.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mac: do not skip a trailing DevStatusReq after LinkADRReq

ProcessMacCommands() post-incremented past the next CID after a LinkADRReq
block and only stepped back when macIndex < commandsSize. A 1-byte command
that is the last FOpts byte right after the block (DevStatusReq, as ChirpStack
sends it) was therefore never processed and DevStatusAns never sent.
Peek at the next CID instead.

hardwario/sticker-firmware#419
---
diff --git a/src/mac/LoRaMac.c b/src/mac/LoRaMac.c
index b0b1fb71..f0e3de91 100644
--- a/src/mac/LoRaMac.c
+++ b/src/mac/LoRaMac.c
@@ -2207,6 +2207,7 @@ static void ProcessMacCommands( uint8_t *payload, uint8_t macIndex, uint8_t comm
                 int8_t linkAdrTxPower = TX_POWER_0;
                 uint8_t linkAdrNbRep = 0;
                 uint8_t linkAdrNbBytesParsed = 0;
+                bool nextIsLinkAdrReq = false;
 
                 // The end node is allowed to process one block of LinkAdrRequests.
                 // It must ignore subsequent blocks
@@ -2274,13 +2275,19 @@ static void ProcessMacCommands( uint8_t *payload, uint8_t macIndex, uint8_t comm
                         if( macIndex >= commandsSize )
                             break;
 
-                    } while( payload[macIndex++] == SRV_MAC_LINK_ADR_REQ );
-
-                    if( macIndex < commandsSize )
-                    {
-                        // Decrease the index such that it points to the next MAC command
-                        macIndex--;
-                    }
+                        // STICKER-419: peek at the next CID instead of post-incrementing
+                        // past it. The old "while( payload[macIndex++] == ... )" plus a
+                        // trailing "if( macIndex < commandsSize ) macIndex--" skipped a
+                        // 1-byte command that is the last FOpts byte right after the
+                        // LinkADRReq block (DevStatusReq), so DevStatusAns was never sent.
+                        nextIsLinkAdrReq = ( payload[macIndex] == SRV_MAC_LINK_ADR_REQ );
+                        if( nextIsLinkAdrReq == true )
+                        {
+                            // Keep the "Payload = &payload[macIndex - 1]" convention
+                            macIndex++;
+                        }
+                    } while( nextIsLinkAdrReq == true );
+                    // macIndex now points at the next MAC command (or past the end)
                 }
                 else
                 {
